#
# Golden fixture builders (WI-0.093). They are long straight-line code that fills one table field per line, so
# the per-function complexity limit (which counts every ternary and loop) says nothing useful here. The schema's
# `byte`/`int8` fields are small signed numbers (QP, reference index, sentinel -1), not characters, so the two
# signed-char checks only produce noise on every assignment. The spec structs give every member an initializer
# on purpose: GCC's -Wmissing-field-initializers (an error under -Werror) fires on designated initializers
# that leave out a member without one. inspect_json.cpp calls the generated UnPackTo(): Apple clang's analyzer
# reports clang-analyzer-cplusplus.NewDeleteLeaks inside that flatc-generated code (unique_ptr members assigned
# from a fresh allocation), a false positive in code we do not write (same override as core/tests/model/).
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-signed-char-misuse,
  -cert-str34-c,
  -readability-redundant-member-init,
  -clang-analyzer-cplusplus.NewDeleteLeaks
CheckOptions:
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.Threshold: 120
